      "signature": "FILE * ParseModeAndOpenFile(LPCSTR lpszFilePath, char * szMode, uint dwPermissions, FILE * pFileHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Parses fopen() style mode string and opens a file with specified permissions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read first character of mode string to determine base access mode\n2. Set dwOpenFlags based on 'r' (read), 'w' (write/create), 'a' (append)\n3. Set dwFileFlags with read/write bits from g_dwDefaultFileFlags\n4. Parse additional mode characters in loop:\n   - '+' enables read+write mode (0x80 flag)\n   - 'b' sets binary mode (0x8000)\n   - 't' sets text mode (0x4000)\n   - 'T' sets temporary file (0x1000)\n   - 'D' sets delete-on-close (0x40)\n   - 'R' sets random access hint (0x10)\n   - 'S' sets sequential access hint (0x20)\n   - 'c' enables commit mode (0x4000 in flags)\n   - 'n' disables commit mode\n5. Call internal open function with parsed flags\n6. If successful, initialize FILE structure fields and increment open file count\n7. Return pointer to FILE structure or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n- lpszFilePath (LPCSTR): Path to the file to open\n- szMode (char*): fopen-style mode string (r/w/a with optional b/t/+/etc)\n- dwPermissions (uint): File permission flags for creation\n- pFileHandle (FILE*): Pre-allocated FILE structure to populate\n\nReturns:\n- FILE* pointer to populated structure on success\n- NULL (0x0) on invalid mode or open failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x109: Append mode flags (O_CREAT | O_APPEND)\n- 0x301: Write mode flags (O_CREAT | O_TRUNC | O_WRONLY)\n- 0x1a4: Default file permissions (octal 0644)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
