      "name": "UnlockFileHandle",
      "signature": "void UnlockFileHandle(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Releases file lock for FILE structure during stream initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract FILE pointer from caller's stack frame at [EBP - 0x1c]\n2. Call __unlock_file() to release critical section lock on FILE._lock\n3. Return via __stdcall convention (callee cleans stack)\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT FILE* - Pointer to FILE structure from caller's stack at [EBP - 0x1c]\n                 The FILE structure has a critical section lock at offset +32\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, performs lock cleanup only\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis is a code factorization wrapper extracted to reduce duplication in file I/O paths.\nThe FILE pointer is accessed via the caller's base pointer (EBP), not passed as a\nstandard parameter, indicating this function executes within the caller's stack frame.\nCalled exclusively from __fsopen() after __openfile() completes stream initialization.\n\nThe __unlock_file() callee determines whether the FILE is in the static I/O buffer\npool (0x6ff7e33f to 0x6ff7e5a1) or dynamically allocated, then releases the\nappropriate critical section accordingly.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5f97d76a7bf7bad4437ec948fbad99b7",
