      "comment": "Flushes OS file buffers for a file descriptor and handles error reporting through thread-local errno.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file descriptor against g_dwMaxFileDescriptor limit\n2. If invalid, set errno to EBADF (0x9) and return -1\n3. Calculate stride offset: (fdFile & 0x1f) * 0x24 for validation array access\n4. Load validation bitmap from g_FileDescriptorTable[fdFile >> 5]\n5. Test bit 0 of validation byte at [bitmap + 4 + stride] to check if descriptor active\n6. If not active, jump to error handler\n7. Lock file descriptor using __lock_fhandle(fdFile) to prevent concurrent access\n8. Re-verify file descriptor validity after lock acquired (race condition check)\n9. If still valid, obtain OS file handle via __get_osfhandle(fdFile)\n10. Call Windows FlushFileBuffers API to flush file buffers to disk\n11. Check flush result: 0=failure (GetLastError), non-zero=success\n12. If error occurred, retrieve Windows error code and store in thread-local errno\n13. If no error, errorCode remains 0\n14. Unlock file descriptor via __unlock_fhandle(fdFile)\n15. Return errorCode: 0 on success, system error code on Windows API failure, -1 (0xffffffff) on validation/locking failure\n\nParameters:\nfdFile (uint) - File descriptor to flush, typically obtained from FILE structure _file member (0-based index into descriptor table)\n\nReturns:\nint - 0 on successful flush, system error code (non-zero DWORD) if Windows API failed, -1 (0xffffffff) if descriptor invalid or locking failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- File descriptors are validated through a bitmap array where bit 0 indicates active status\n- Validation is performed twice: before and after acquiring lock to detect descriptor closure during lock wait\n- Stride calculation (fd & 0x1f) * 0x24 suggests up to 32 descriptors per table entry, each with 0x24 bytes storage\n- EBADF (0x9) is standard POSIX error for bad file descriptor\n- Thread-local errno access via GetThreadErrorNumberPointer() supports multi-threaded error handling\n- Lock/unlock pair ensures atomic flush operation without descriptor state corruption",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:843e3db8ac5607bba3d919f4ee9bcace",
